{"absent":["How and when package width globals, threading maximum, frequency scale and capacity values are initialized or updated, and what synchronization protects them.","Full layouts of per CPU topology records, mask objects, register frame flags field, and supervisor mapping state.","Behavior of supervisor access allow, revoke, save and restore primitives and of exception table fault redirection beyond the need for a caller fault path.","Payload layout, enablement and ordering guarantees of floating point, hypervisor and vector trace events.","Locking, sleeping and interrupt context constraints for topology queries, frequency helpers and user memory transfers.","Handling of malformed, unmapped or out of range user addresses, including exact error values observed by callers."],"dossier":"D10","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_max_dies_per_package","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_num_cores_per_package","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_num_threads_per_package","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_num_nodes_per_package"],"text":"Package sizing queries expose stored counts for dies, cores, hardware threads and nodes contained in one package, letting callers size topology iteration without recomputing hardware enumeration."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_get_logical_id"],"text":"Lookup of a logical identifier from an APIC value at a requested topology level is offered in a degenerate shape that uniformly reports zero."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_cluster_id","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_die_cpumask","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_cluster_cpumask","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_core_cpumask","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_sibling_cpumask"],"text":"Topology grouping access gives the cluster number from per CPU records together with die, cluster, core and sibling membership sets for a given processor."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_phys_to_logical_pkg.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_phys_to_logical_pkg.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_max_smt_threads.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_max_smt_threads.alt_2"],"text":"Physical to logical package mapping and threading depth each have dual shapes: one translating through system domain configuration or stored state, and one constant fallback reporting zero or a single thread."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::cpu_primary_thread_mask","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_is_primary_thread.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_is_primary_thread.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_is_core_online.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::topology_is_core_online.alt_2"],"text":"Primary thread identity is shared as a global mask with a membership predicate, and core online state follows the online state of the related primary thread, treating missing primaries as offline."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::arch_fix_phys_package_id"],"text":"Correction of the physical package identifier for a processor and slot is specified as a no operation with no visible state change."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::sysctl_sched_itmt_enabled","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::sched_set_itmt_core_prio","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::sched_set_itmt_support","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::sched_clear_itmt_support"],"text":"Throughput management hints are reported as unsupported through a disabled flag, empty priority and clear actions, and a support probe that indicates absence."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::arch_scale_freq_invariant","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::arch_scale_freq_capacity.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::arch_scale_freq_capacity.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::arch_scale_cpu_capacity","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::arch_enable_hybrid_capacity_scale","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::arch_set_cpu_capacity","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::arch_set_max_freq_ratio","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::freq_invariance_set_perf_ratio","arch/x86/include/asm/topology.h::arch_scale_freq_tick"],"text":"Capacity scaling exposes an invariance predicate, per processor current capacity retrieval, and disabled hybrid handling with empty setters for capacity, frequency ratio and performance ratio."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trace/fpu.h::TRACE_SYSTEM","arch/x86/include/asm/trace/hyperv.h::TRACE_SYSTEM","arch/x86/include/asm/trace/irq_vectors.h::TRACE_SYSTEM"],"text":"Trace subsystems declare separate system identities for floating point activity, hypervisor activity and interrupt vector activity."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trace/irq_vectors.h::DEFINE_IRQ_VECTOR_EVENT","arch/x86/include/asm/trace/irq_vectors.h::DEFINE_IRQ_VECTOR_MOD_EVENT","arch/x86/include/asm/trace/irq_vectors.h::DEFINE_IRQ_VECTOR_RESERVE_EVENT","arch/x86/include/asm/trace/irq_vectors.h::DEFINE_IRQ_VECTOR_ACTIVATE_EVENT"],"text":"Vector tracing constructors generate paired entry and exit probes keyed by vector number, plus distinct probes for vector migration with old and new placement, for reservation results, and for activation policy flags."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trace_clock.h::ARCH_TRACE_CLOCKS"],"text":"Architecture trace time offers one clock derived from the processor cycle counter whose values are raw counter ticks rather than nanoseconds."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trap_pf.h::x86_pf_error_code"],"text":"Fault cause encoding assigns the lowest six bit positions in order to protection failure, write access, user mode, reserved bit misuse, instruction fetch and key protection failure."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trap_pf.h::x86_pf_error_code"],"text":"The same fault encoding places a shadow stack indication above the low group and places virtualization related indications at the fifteenth and thirty first bit positions."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::EVENT_TYPE_EXTINT","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::EVENT_TYPE_RESERVED","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::EVENT_TYPE_NMI","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::EVENT_TYPE_HWEXC","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::EVENT_TYPE_SWINT"],"text":"Event source numbering starts with external interrupts at zero, leaves one reserved, then orders non maskable interrupts, hardware exceptions and software interrupts on the next three values."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::EVENT_TYPE_PRIV_SWEXC","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::EVENT_TYPE_SWEXC","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::EVENT_TYPE_OTHER"],"text":"Remaining event source numbers assign privileged software exceptions, general software exceptions and a miscellaneous class covering fast system entry and virtualization traps to the next three values."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_DE","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_DB","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_NMI","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_BP","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_OF","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_BR"],"text":"Trap numbering begins with divide error at zero and continues through debug, non maskable, breakpoint, overflow and bound range conditions on the following five values."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_UD","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_NM","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_DF","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_OLD_MF","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_TS","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_NP"],"text":"The next six trap numbers in order cover invalid opcode, unavailable device, double fault, legacy coprocessor overrun, invalid task state and missing segment."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_SS","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_GP","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_PF","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_SPURIOUS","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_MF"],"text":"Following trap numbers in order cover stack fault, general protection, page fault, spurious interrupt and floating point error."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_AC","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_MC","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_XF","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_VE","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_CP"],"text":"Subsequent consecutive trap numbers cover alignment checking, machine checking, vector floating point, virtualization and control protection conditions."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_VC","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::X86_TRAP_IRET"],"text":"Two sparse trap numbers place virtual machine communication well above the dense range and interrupt return handling at thirty two."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/traps.h::get_si_code"],"text":"Debug status translation gives precedence to single stepping, then to any hardware breakpoint indication, and otherwise reports a software breakpoint."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/traps.h::cond_local_irq_enable","arch/x86/include/asm/traps.h::cond_local_irq_disable"],"text":"Interrupt state helpers change processor interrupt allowance only when the saved processor flags show that interrupts were previously permitted, otherwise leaving state untouched."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/tsc.h::cycles_t"],"text":"Cycle count values are carried as unsigned sixty four bit integers."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/tsc.h::get_cycles.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/tsc.h::get_cycles.alt_2"],"text":"Cycle counter reading yields zero when the counter feature is unavailable and otherwise yields the live hardware counter."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__uaccess_begin","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__uaccess_end","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::user_access_save","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::user_access_restore"],"text":"User access regions are bracketed by supervisor access allow and revoke primitives, with save and restore of the surrounding protection state delegated to supervisor mapping helpers."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::get_user","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::put_user","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::do_get_user_call","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::do_put_user_call"],"text":"Checked user loads and stores form callable transfer points that record possible faulting before delegating to size specialized call helpers whose zero result means success."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__put_user_size","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_size.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_size.alt_2"],"text":"User transfer size handling accepts only one, two, four and eight byte widths and diverts every other width to an invalid size path."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::arch_unsafe_put_user","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::arch_unsafe_get_user.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::arch_unsafe_get_user.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__put_user_goto","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__put_user_goto_u64.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__put_user_goto_u64.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_asm.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_asm.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_asm_u64.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_asm_u64.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_asm_u64.alt_3","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_asm_u64.alt_4","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_size.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_size.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__put_user_size"],"text":"Unchecked user loads and stores operate inside an already opened window and on fault either jump to a caller supplied label or record an error for the caller to test."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__large_struct","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__m","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::movsl_mask.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::movsl_mask.alt_2"],"text":"User memory operands are modeled with a dummy aggregate holding one hundred machine words, and optimized copying consults a cache line aligned object containing a single integer mask."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::ARCH_HAS_NONTEMPORAL_UACCESS","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::copy_mc_to_kernel"],"text":"The build claims support for non temporal user accesses with a positive flag and advertises machine check tolerant copying to kernel memory under its own name."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::unsafe_try_cmpxchg_user","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__try_cmpxchg_user","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__try_cmpxchg_user_asm.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__try_cmpxchg_user_asm.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__try_cmpxchg64_user_asm.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__try_cmpxchg64_user_asm.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__try_cmpxchg64_user_asm.alt_3"],"text":"User atomic compare exchange selects among byte, word, double word and quad word forms, writes back the observed value on mismatch, and reports success as a boolean."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__try_cmpxchg_user_asm.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__try_cmpxchg_user_asm.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__try_cmpxchg64_user_asm.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__try_cmpxchg64_user_asm.alt_2"],"text":"User compare exchange operations execute with bus locking semantics so the comparison and conditional update appear atomic to other processors."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__put_user_goto","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_asm.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_asm.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::do_get_user_call","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::do_put_user_call"],"text":"All user memory operations depend on exception fixup entries, so every use must supply a reachable fault path and must not assume any value was transferred after a fault."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__put_user_goto_u64.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_asm_u64.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__get_user_asm_u64.alt_3"],"text":"Narrow implementations transfer eight byte user values as two independent four byte halves, allowing torn reads or writes under concurrency and requiring separate fault handling per half."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__inttype","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::__typefits"],"text":"Temporary storage for user values chooses the narrowest unsigned character, short, integer or long type whose size covers the accessed object."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trace/fpu.h::_TRACE_FPU_H","arch/x86/include/asm/trace/hyperv.h::_TRACE_HYPERV_H","arch/x86/include/asm/trace/irq_vectors.h::_TRACE_IRQ_VECTORS_H","arch/x86/include/asm/trace_clock.h::_ASM_X86_TRACE_CLOCK_H","arch/x86/include/asm/trap_pf.h::_ASM_X86_TRAP_PF_H","arch/x86/include/asm/trapnr.h::_ASM_X86_TRAPNR_H","arch/x86/include/asm/traps.h::_ASM_X86_TRAPS_H","arch/x86/include/asm/tsc.h::_ASM_X86_TSC_H","arch/x86/include/asm/uaccess.h::_ASM_X86_UACCESS_H"],"text":"Each header establishes a single inclusion guard macro that suppresses repeated inclusion within one compilation."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/trace/fpu.h::TRACE_INCLUDE_PATH","arch/x86/include/asm/t